attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `selB`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0.4% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.05 bits {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at column 1**, `yiaY`, carried by 90%, in a region of plasticity in 92% of calls {S2, S2.c1}. Then columns 3 to 17, fork and variable, carried by 54 to 89%, hold `yiaW` to `yiaJ`, [[gulonate catabolism]] at columns 10 to 16 {S4, S4.c12-17, Q}. A second branch of 3 families runs through columns 8 to 10, carried by 33 to 35%, [[glycoside hydrolase and transport]] {S4.b8}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 93 against 90%, and hesitates less there, 0.21 against 0.33 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 3, a fork column, is at 0.98 bits {H, M}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 73 to 79, `yhjB` to `mdtF`, are carried by 59 to 89%, all persistent {S14}. The last column is `mdtF`, in 59% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 92% of genes**, 0.26 bits on average, perplexity 1.5 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.42 against 0.18 bits, and names about as many genes, 90% against 93% {C}.

